Package: oshioki
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: amd64
Maintainer: Oshioki contributors
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Depends: adduser, file, sudo, init-system-helpers
Description: Touch ID or WebAuthn approval for sudo requests
 Oshioki asks an enrolled device to approve one exact sudo request.
 The hook encrypts the request for each enrolled device; the server
 stores routing data and ciphertext. Devices approve from a browser
 via WebAuthn or from the native agent via Secure Enclave.
